{"stream":"c5-security","type":"finding","confidence":"high","topic":"Security concern: auto-update","finding":"nsync-gui fetches raw script from GitHub (REMOTE_URL) and overwrites itself without any signature verification. Supply chain attack vector: if GitHub account is compromised, all nsync-gui instances auto-update to malicious code."}
{"stream":"c2-infra","type":"finding","confidence":"high","topic":"IAM scope gap","finding":"IAM role config-sync-auth-role uses bucket.grantReadWrite(authRole) — grants s3:GetObject, s3:PutObject, s3:DeleteObject, s3:ListBucket on entire bucket. Any authenticated Cognito user can read/write/delete any key including other users' pending/ objects. No per-user path restriction."}
{"stream":"c4-scripts","type":"finding","confidence":"medium","topic":"nsync-genpass region hardcode","finding":"nsync-genpass hardcodes region_name='us-west-2' for Bedrock. Will fail if user's AWS account doesn't have Bedrock access in us-west-2 or if they prefer a different region. Should use cfg['region'] or a configurable default."}
{"stream":"c3-approval","type":"finding","confidence":"medium","topic":"pass-nsync.bash import-pass behavior","finding":"pass-nsync.bash calls 'nsync import-pass' after every pass insert/edit/generate/rm. import-pass re-imports the ENTIRE pass store each time (walks ~/.password-store, decrypts all .gpg files). Slow for large stores and makes unnecessary Cognito auth calls."}
{"stream":"c1-cli","type":"finding","confidence":"high","topic":"Missing from agent prompt","finding":"Agent prompt missing: (1) all 5 scripts and their purposes, (2) nsync-genpass Bedrock dependency, (3) stealth naming convention (config-sync-* not nsync-*), (4) version history feature in store, (5) 3650-day refresh token for trusted devices, (6) test suite (pytest in cli/tests/), (7) generate-setup.sh for device onboarding, (8) nsync_picker.py bug."}
